{
  "task_description": "{'component_name': 'Main Container for VintageChrono', 'description': "Primary container for VintageChrono implementation: PastBlast is a responsive web app that lets users explore historical events for any date, styled with a vintage newspaper aesthetic. It integrates Wikipedia's 'On This Day' API to display notable events, and optionally NYT Archive and Archive.org for period headlines and imagery. Features include a rotary date picker, timeline slider, wax seal/typewriter key buttons, and interactive elements like 'Random Year' and 'My Birth Year'. The UI uses parchment backgrounds, classic fonts, and ink/antique gold accents, with responsive layouts and accessible, semantic HTML.", 'framework': 'react', 'platform': 'web', 'container': '{\n  "name": "ColorCraft frontend Container",\n  "features": [\n    {\n      "name": "Date Picker",\n      "description": "A rotary or brass dial styled date picker allowing users to select any day, month, and year. Defaults to today\\u2019s date.",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "Timeline Slider",\n      "description": "A pocket-watch face styled slider to quickly browse through years or decades.",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "Historical Events Feed",\n      "description": "Displays 5\\u201310 notable events from Wikipedia\'s \'On This Day\' API for the selected date, shown as newspaper clipping cards or accordions.",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "NYT Archive Headlines",\n      "description": "Shows 2\\u20133 headlines from the New York Times Archive API for the selected month/year, styled as newsprint cutouts with source links and thumbnails.",\n      "isEnabled": false\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "Random Year Button",\n      "description": "A \'\\ud83c\\udfb2 Random Year\' button that jumps to a surprise date and fetches events.",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "My Birth Year Feature",\n      "description": "A \'\\ud83d\\udcdc My Birth Year\' feature that fetches info based on user-inputted birth date.",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "Sound Toggle",\n      "description": "Toggle for vintage typewriter clicks or phonograph music.",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "Loading Animation",\n      "description": "Paper flipping or quill writing animation during data fetches.",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "Responsive Design",\n      "description": "Fully responsive layout for desktop, tablet, and mobile devices.",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    }\n  ],\n  "techStack": {\n    "frontend": [\n      "React JS"\n    ],\n    "backend": [\n      "None"\n    ],\n    "language": [\n      "JavaScript (ES6+)"\n    ]\n  },\n  "colors": {\n    "primary": "#2f2f2f",\n    "secondary": "#6a4e42",\n    "accent": "#bfa77a"\n  },\n  "theme": "light",\n  "layoutDescription": "The UI features a parchment-textured background with faded paper borders and subtle creases. At the top, a bold, vintage-style header uses \'Cormorant Garamond\' or \'Playfair Display\'. Below, a rotary date picker and pocket-watch timeline slider allow date selection. Main content area displays event cards styled as newspaper clippings, with accordions for details. NYT headlines (if enabled) appear as newsprint cutouts with thumbnails. Buttons resemble wax seals or typewriter keys, with smudged ink hover effects. Footer includes sound toggle and credits. All components are spaced for readability and adapt fluidly to screen size."\n}'}",
